  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-mcp-servers — MCP servers settings page",
      "text": "[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@railgun52/dsh-mcp-servers)\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n> A profile-config settings page for DeepSeek Harness that lets you manage MCP servers from the Web UI and mounts live `mcp-client` instances from the saved list."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-mcp-servers — MCP servers settings page",
      "text": "Each server you add becomes a running MCP client whose tools are registered on the agent tool registry, so the model can call them the moment you save — no restart, no hand-edited YAML. The page is a JSON editor over the `mcp-servers` profile-config namespace; the Host half owns the schema and the live bridge, the browser half owns the editor card."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "| Feature | Description |\n|---|---|\n| Settings page | A first-level Settings section `MCP 服务器` with an add/edit/remove card list |\n| JSON editor | Edit the whole `servers` array in one textarea; add a server with one click |\n| Live bridge | The Host mounts one `mcp-client` instance per enabled server and re-syncs on every settings edit (`loader/volatile-update`) without remounting the plugin |\n| stdio + streamable-http | Each server carries `name`, `command`, `args`, `env`, `transport`, `url`, `enabled` |\n| Profile-config backed | Values persist to the active profile's plugin config; the page reads/writes through the shared `configForms` namespace |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture",
      "text": "```text\ndsh-mcp-servers/\n|-- src/\n|   |-- index.ts               # host half: Config schema (volatile servers) + mcp-client bridge\n|   |-- mcp-servers-schema.ts  # McpServersSchema + McpServerConfig"
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture",
      "text": "- **Namespace**: `mcp-servers`. The owning profile entry id must equal this string; the plugin's Config schema IS the namespace under the profile-config settings model.\n- **Live edits**: `servers` is declared `.volatile()`, so the settings model exposes the namespace and edits do not remount the plugin. The Host reads the live value through `Volatile.get()` and re-syncs the bridge on `loader/volatile-update`.\n- **Browser bundle**: rides the `window.__ModuleLoader__.load` contract; React and `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-primitives` resolve from the loader's module table (external); CSS Modules are inlined by lightningcss as `<style data-plugin>`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "From a local directory (development)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add link:/absolute/path/to/dsh-mcp-servers"
    },
    {
      "section": "From npm (recommended)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add @railgun52/dsh-mcp-servers@latest\n```\n\nAfter installing, **restart `dsh web`**. Open Settings → MCP 服务器 to manage servers. In link mode, run `pnpm build` and refresh the page after a code change; no reinstall needed."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm install\npnpm build        # tsc -b (types+declarations) && tsdown (node half + browser bundle)\npnpm typecheck    # type check only\n```\n\nThe browser bundle is produced with the harness `clientBundle` helper; building from a fresh clone requires the DeepSeek Harness repository available (the `tsdown.config.ts` imports its `clientBundle`). The shipped `lib/` is pre-built, so consumers never build."
    },
    {
